    ":question/id": "8dcd24a2-ce5f-5ab6-8a92-814e8f1355a9",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-29662",
    ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Note that $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/2}}={x}^{-5/2}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}} & =\\int {x}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/2+1}}{-\\frac{5}{2}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-3/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3{x}^{3/2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
